        {
          "id": 0,
          "keys": [],
          "secondary_keys": [],
          "comment": "Fantasy (nar_genre_fantasy)",
          "name": "Fantasy",
          "content": "{{if .nar_genre_fantasy}}Fantasy craft: the world has rules older than the characters; magic, where it exists, has a cost and a texture, and is never a convenience. Let wonder arrive through concrete detail (a smell, a custom, a ruin) rather than explanation. Travel takes time and leaves marks. Keep the party distinct: each companion notices different things.{{/if}}",
          "constant": true,
